<https://w3id.org/arknet/model/ubiquitous-language> {
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/24b5563d-4f98-4884-b08b-9aa75af41917> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "TERM-25";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/arknet/model/glossary>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Ubiquitous Language"@de, "Ubiquitous Language"@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Die Ubiquitous Language ist die eine Sprache, die Fachleute und Entwickler innerhalb eines Bounded Context gemeinsam sprechen und die sich in Gesprächen, Modell und Code unverändert wiederfindet: jedes Wort hat darin genau eine Bedeutung, und was im Gespräch so heißt, heißt im Modell genauso. Sie ist an ihren Bounded Context gebunden; jenseits seiner Grenze gilt eine andere."@de,
      "The Ubiquitous Language is the one language that domain experts and developers speak together within a Bounded Context and that appears unchanged in conversation, model and code: every word has exactly one meaning in it, and what is called something in conversation is called the same in the model. It is bound to its Bounded Context; beyond that boundary a different one applies."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/c2df3868-3a66-46ca-8621-677374d02aa6>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/7c1ae58a-a7db-4e10-b567-c333f14fb9c9> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/d6f351d9-ec26-4041-95f9-77059a89090d> a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "TERM-26";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/arknet/model/glossary>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Component"@de, "Component"@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Eine oder mehrere Komponenten bilden einen Bounded Context und sprechen dessen Ubiquitous Language. Jede Komponente hat ihre eigene Zuständigkeit und gruppiert zusammengehörige Funktionalität hinter einer Schnittstelle."@de,
      "One or more Components form a Bounded Context and speak its Ubiquitous Language. Each Component has a responsibility of its own and groups related functionality behind an interface."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/7c1ae58a-a7db-4e10-b567-c333f14fb9c9>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/24b5563d-4f98-4884-b08b-9aa75af41917> .
}

<https://w3id.org/arknet/model/bounded-context> {
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/e6ba4963-8b0c-4e13-aec9-b0ec72fc4496> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#BoundedContext>;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "BC-1";
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/core#name> "Produkt & Anforderungen"@de, "Product & Requirements"@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#domainVision> "Hält fest, was das beschriebene System leisten soll: Anforderungen mit Akzeptanzkriterien, die von außen gesetzten Constraints und die Use Cases, in denen Rollen das System nutzen."@de,
      "Records what the described system is to deliver: requirements with acceptance criteria, the externally imposed constraints, and the use cases in which roles use the system."@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#partOf> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/4c28655e-6829-43a3-910d-0398c12fb028>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#ubiquitousLanguageTerm> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/0c5ff58a-96c6-4143-80e2-683586edf6e8>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/87ab2eca-efa7-4067-be38-103b0ab6f299> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/804ade54-7c54-45d1-804d-d0db6dc2a114> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#BoundedContext>;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "BC-2";
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/core#name> "Domänenmodellierung"@de, "Domain Modelling"@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#domainVision> "Führt Sprache und Grenzen des Modells: die Begriffe, in denen die Ubiquitous Language festgehalten wird, sowie die Bounded Contexts mit ihren Context-Map-Beziehungen."@de,
      "Keeps the model's language and boundaries: the terms in which the Ubiquitous Language is written down, and the Bounded Contexts with their context-map relationships."@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#partOf> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/eb77d14a-52f6-47dc-aa2c-93dffc6c7621>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#ubiquitousLanguageTerm> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/c2df3868-3a66-46ca-8621-677374d02aa6>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/7c1ae58a-a7db-4e10-b567-c333f14fb9c9>, <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/24b5563d-4f98-4884-b08b-9aa75af41917>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/d6f351d9-ec26-4041-95f9-77059a89090d> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/a6870e28-4aa0-4cf5-86da-f8a1fb1f9c70> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#BoundedContext>;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "BC-3";
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/core#name> "Architektur & Entscheidungen"@de, "Architecture & Decisions"@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#domainVision> "Hält fest, wie das System gebaut wird: Architekturentscheidungen als Records mit Kontext, Folgen und erwogenen Optionen, verknüpft mit den Anforderungen, Kontexten und Begriffen, die sie betreffen."@de,
      "Records how the system is built: architecture decisions as records with context, consequences and considered options, linked to the requirements, contexts and terms they touch."@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#partOf> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/2cbef2c6-0d89-47fc-9045-bf2881d836ef> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/2f2943e7-0df6-4238-8a59-99606852aa36> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#BoundedContext>;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "BC-4";
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/core#name> "Actor"@en, "Akteur"@de;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#domainVision> "Führt das Register der Akteure, die auf das System wirken oder ein Interesse an ihm haben, und der Rollen, die sie ausfüllen, damit Anforderungen und Use Cases auf sie verweisen können."@de,
      "Keeps the register of the actors that act on the system or hold an interest in it, and of the roles they fill, so that requirements and use cases can refer to them."@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#partOf> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/d895d408-c762-4f38-9cb3-6410d637f030>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#ubiquitousLanguageTerm> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/803ccddc-e007-40f8-bf43-57485cdca551>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/5534b165-fa1e-4a74-b725-73058fcb4853>, <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/d92fadcd-2213-4e54-a1fc-2ae5cc508466>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/f244f238-5f56-4e7c-b20e-8c7473bc0637>, <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/d725f1e3-922c-4597-a58b-4b5060de1e48>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/b585160f-4f80-4baa-aa6b-8178666bb635> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/1d06bb6f-847d-409e-b024-23081ffb9c43> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#BoundedContext>;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "BC-5";
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/core#name> "Projekt-Registry"@de, "Project Registry"@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#domainVision> "Bildet den Anker eines Aufrufs auf das registrierte Projekt ab und führt dessen Identität, Anker und Sprachzusagen, stromaufwärts von jedem anderen Kontext."@de,
      "Maps the anchor of a call to the registered project and keeps that project's identity, anchors and language commitments, upstream of every other context."@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#partOf> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/b2360925-2bdf-4d8f-9c7b-f0905784c262>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#ubiquitousLanguageTerm> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/ebdd226f-5b5d-46b6-a41a-53ec10c2090c>,
      <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/8fc7d040-da89-4b17-9aff-5d557709088a> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/b96f19b0-a38f-4c76-9064-02912d10e8f5> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#BoundedContext>;
    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "BC-6";
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/core#name> "Modellanalyse"@de, "Model Analysis"@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#domainVision> "Wertet das Modell lesend über Kontextgrenzen hinweg aus: Auswirkungen, Nachverfolgbarkeit, verwaiste Ressourcen, Rollen-Use-Case-Matrix, Begriffs-Kookkurrenz und Sprachlücken; schreibt nie."@de,
      "Evaluates the model read-only across context boundaries: impact, traceability, orphaned resources, the role/use-case matrix, term co-occurrence and language gaps; it never writes."@en;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#partOf> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/b8ed4eed-5c7d-43c1-a506-70152cbaa5a7> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/2cbef2c6-0d89-47fc-9045-bf2881d836ef> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#Subdomain>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#subdomainType> <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#CoreDomain> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/b8ed4eed-5c7d-43c1-a506-70152cbaa5a7> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#Subdomain>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#subdomainType> <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#SupportingDomain> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/9e707310-3b4e-44c6-bc44-8ce620835b1e> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#ContextRelationship>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#upstream> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/804ade54-7c54-45d1-804d-d0db6dc2a114>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#downstream> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/e6ba4963-8b0c-4e13-aec9-b0ec72fc4496>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#relationshipType> <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#PublishedLanguage> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/e142272d-fb21-40b2-a3ab-8fc15917d8dd> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#ContextRelationship>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#upstream> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/2f2943e7-0df6-4238-8a59-99606852aa36>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#downstream> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/e6ba4963-8b0c-4e13-aec9-b0ec72fc4496>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#relationshipType> <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#PublishedLanguage> .
  
  <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/7561183c-dcae-4b07-8ae9-0c70e22d7a82> a <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#ContextRelationship>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#upstream> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/e6ba4963-8b0c-4e13-aec9-b0ec72fc4496>;
    <https://w3id.org/arknet/ddd#downstream> <https://w3id.org/arknet/id/a6870e28-4aa0-4cf5-86da-f8a1fb1f9c70>;
